## Testing Types

## Test Pyramid

```
           /\
          /E2E\ ← fewest, slowest, most fragile
         /──────\
        /Integr.  \ ← medium, slower, catch wiring
       /────────────\
      /  Unit Tests   \ ← most, fastest, catch logic
     /──────────────────\
```

## Unit Test

```typescript
// Tests one function/class in isolation
// All dependencies are mocked
describe('calculateDiscount', () => {
  it('applies 20% discount for premium users', () => {
    expect(calculateDiscount(100, { isPremium: true })).toBe(80);
  });
});

Speed: milliseconds | Scope: one function | Mocks: yes
```

## Integration Test

```typescript
// Tests components working together — real DB, real service
describe('UserRepository', () => {
  it('saves and retrieves a user', async () => {
    const repo = new SupabaseUserRepository(testDb);
    await repo.save(testUser);
    const found = await repo.findById(testUser.id);
    expect(found).toEqual(testUser);
  });
});

Speed: seconds | Scope: multiple components | Mocks: external only
```

## Smoke Test

```
Run after each deployment:
  1. GET / → 200
  2. POST /api/auth/login → 200
  3. GET /api/products → 200

Fast subset (~2 min) that verifies core paths work.
If smoke tests fail → rollback immediately, don't run full suite.
```

## Regression Test

```typescript
// Documents a bug that was fixed and prevents it from returning
describe('Order total calculation (regression: #JIRA-123)', () => {
  it('does not apply discount twice for bundled products', () => {
    const order = new Order([bundle1, bundle2]);
    expect(order.total()).toBe(90); // was incorrectly 81 before fix
  });
});
```

## Summary

```
Unit        → Is the logic correct in isolation?
Integration → Do components work together?
Smoke       → Is the deployment basically alive?
Regression  → Does old behaviour still work after new changes?
```

